{
  // Issue #361 (S312 fix-now round, red-team finding F5): tsconfig.json's own "include" is
  // "src/**/*.ts" only, so the 3 production enforcement hooks (plain `.mjs` Node ESM scripts,
  // hooks/pretooluse-kernel-gate.mjs, hooks/sessionstart-tool-enum.mjs,
  // hooks/userpromptsubmit-halt-relay.mjs — the actual PreToolUse/SessionStart/UserPromptSubmit
  // call sites) were NEVER typechecked. Dropping a required argument (e.g.
  // renderHookOutput's `sanitize` port) gave `npm run build` rc=0; only ESLint's incidental
  // no-unused-vars catch on the now-dead import binding caught it, and only when the binding
  // happened to become unused.
  //
  // A separate project file, not a widened `include` on tsconfig.json, for the same reason
  // eslint.config.mjs already lints `hooks/**/*.mjs` in its own file block, deliberately apart from
  // `src/**/*.ts` (see that file's header comment): `hooks/**/*.ts` (the test files and test-support
  // helpers under hooks/) stay OUT of this project too, same lane-scoping precedent — test-writer's
  // and story-implementer's own test files are not pulled into a production-code compile gate, and
  // widening this project to include them risks unrelated pre-existing test-file typecheck noise
  // this fix-now round did not scope in. `checkJs`/`allowJs` are ON here only, not on the base
  // project, so `src/**/*.ts`'s own strict-TS compile is unaffected either way.
  //
  // Covers ALL 3 production enforcement hooks (Issue #361 closed the last gap: the two hooks that
  // used to be excluded here, hooks/sessionstart-tool-enum.mjs and
  // hooks/userpromptsubmit-halt-relay.mjs, were annotated with JSDoc only -- no runtime change,
  // no @ts-ignore/@ts-expect-error/@ts-nocheck -- and now typecheck clean under strict + checkJs,
  // so a dropped required argument or a type mismatch in any of them fails `npm run build` /
  // `npm run typecheck`).
  //
  // `tsconfig.hooks-coverage.json` + `src/qa/hook-typecheck-coverage-check.ts` (CI step "QA-18")
  // stay as a COMPLEMENTARY guard, not a duplicate: QA-18 additionally scans for suppressions no
  // compiler can see, and fails CI if a NEW hook under hooks/ is not covered by a tsconfig project.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["hooks/pretooluse-kernel-gate.mjs", "hooks/sessionstart-tool-enum.mjs", "hooks/userpromptsubmit-halt-relay.mjs"],
  "exclude": ["dist/**", "node_modules/**"]
}
